        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Give the first three in order. (Primero, segundo, tercero.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And what did secundus mean before it meant second? (Following — the one that comes after.) Next: where these words stand, and what happens to two of them when they get there."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C67-primer-libro",
      "sequence": 2547,
      "title": "el primer libro — where an ordinal stands",
      "headword": "el primer libro",
      "romanization": "el primer libro",
      "gloss": "where an ordinal stands, and the shortening you have now seen three times",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:8cd6ebe73d08fa78",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Primero, segundo, tercero. And the rule you have carried for a long time: a Spanish adjective follows its noun."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "These do not."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two things set them apart from ordinary adjectives."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "They go in front. Where grande follows its noun, an ordinal leads: el primer libro, not el libro primero."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And there — did you catch it? Primer, not primero. In front of a masculine singular noun, primero and tercero drop their final o."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "el primer libro, but la primera casa.",
                "el tercer libro, but la tercera casa."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have met this exact habit twice already: mucho to muy, and malo to mal. Three times now, so it is not a set of exceptions — it is what Spanish does to a word leaning on a masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
